\begin{abstract}
Let $K=\QQ(\zeta_7+\zeta_7^{-1})$ be the real cyclic cubic field of conductor $7$, generated by a root of $f(x)=x^3+x^2-2x-1$. We study the decomposition-type channel of $K$: the map sending the residue class of an unramified prime $p$ modulo $7$ to its splitting type, with $p \bmod 7$ uniform on the six invertible classes. We prove: (i) for every prime $p\neq 7$, $f$ has a root modulo $p$ --- equivalently $p$ splits completely with residue degree $1$ --- if and only if $p\equiv\pm1\pmod 7$, and $p$ is inert with residue degree $3$ otherwise, so that only two types occur and the type is a \emph{function} of the residue; (ii) the type entropy is $H(T)=\log_2 3-2/3=0.918296\ldots$ bits and $I(p\bmod 7;T)=H(T)$ exactly (\emph{full pinning}), proved both by closed-form computation and structurally from a general principle that a joint law supported on the graph of a function saturates the data-processing ceiling $I\le H(Y)$; (iii) for a semiprime $N=pq$ with independent uniform factors, the residue $N\bmod 7$ transmits $\log_2 3-10/9=0.473851\ldots$ bits about the unordered pair of factor types, and the deficit from the ceiling is \emph{exactly} $H(T)$ --- multiplication destroys precisely one type label; (iv) although the ordered type pair carries $4/9$ bits more entropy than the unordered one, the residue transmits exactly the same information about both, so the which-factor information is exactly zero, by an exact swap symmetry. We also record the conductor-free mechanism behind (i): an order-$m$ element of $SL_2(\FF_p)$ exists if and only if $m\mid p^2-1$, which specialises to the Fibonacci criterion at conductor $5$, the cubic criterion at $7$, and a quintic criterion at $11$.
\end{abstract}

\noindent\textbf{Keywords:} cyclic cubic field, splitting law, Chebotarev density, mutual information, Shannon entropy, semiprime, data-processing inequality, Chebyshev polynomials.

\section{Introduction}

\subsection{Motivation}

Splitting laws in abelian number fields are usually stated qualitatively: the decomposition type of an unramified prime depends only on its residue class modulo the conductor. That is a statement about determination. It says nothing about \emph{how much} is determined, nor how the determination degrades under natural operations on the input.

We take the quantitative view, treating
\[
p\longmapsto T(p)=\text{decomposition type of }p\text{ in }K
\]
as a communication channel with input $p\bmod m$ and output $T$, and computing its Shannon invariants exactly, in bits, for the simplest cyclic cubic field $K=\QQ(\zeta_7+\zeta_7^{-1})$ of conductor $7$. Three phenomena emerge, all exact expressions in $\log_2 3$ and rationals:
\begin{itemize}
\item the channel attains its information-theoretic ceiling exactly (\emph{full pinning});
\item replacing the prime input by a product of two primes loses information equal, on the nose, to one type entropy;
\item the loss is entirely concentrated in the ``which factor is which'' coordinate, which loses \emph{all} of its information while the multiset coordinate retains the maximum possible.
\end{itemize}

